de since February like you told me, so I have it. I can get a money order from my credit union on Friday morning for the full $4,200 and bring it to the Harbor County Housing Court clerk the same day. Then I'll bring the receipt and a copy of the money order to the clinic so it's in the file.\n[2026-04-29T10:43:00Z] Kofi Mensah: That works. I'd just flag that the $4,200 assumes the court doesn't ask for May's rent to be added before the hearing — if it does, that number goes up.\n[2026-04-29T10:43:00Z] Amara Singh: Noted. We can revisit if the clerk raises it. Decision: $4,200 deposited in escrow with Harbor County Housing Court, Rosa brings the money order proof to the clinic. Kofi, please track the deposit in the case file today.\n[2026-04-29T10:44:00Z] Kofi Mensah: On it.\n[2026-04-29T10:44:00Z] Amara Singh: Last item — hearing timeline. I want to be thoughtful here, because Maplewood's counsel floated the Tenant Mediation Program. If we agree too quickly we lose leverage, and if we refuse outright the court may see us as unreasonable. Where do we land?\n[2026-04-29T10:45:00Z] Rosa Delgado: My preference is to keep the May 14 hearing. They've promised me repairs three times since November and nothing happened. If they actually start fixing things, then I'd be willing to talk in mediation.\n[2026-04-29T10:46:00Z] Kofi Mensah: I like that. Mediation hasn't gone well with this landlord on the last two cases we had against them.\n[2026-04-29T10:46:00Z] Amara Singh: Agreed. Decision: we proceed to the May 14 hearing and decline the Tenant Mediation Program unless repairs actually begin. Rosa, you'll tell Kofi right away if any repair crew shows up?\n[2026-04-29T10:47:00Z] Rosa Delgado: Yes.\n[2026-04-29T10:47:00Z] Amara Singh: And Kofi, you'll coordinate with Hannah on docketing the filing deadline and the hearing date, since she's lining up the filing packet?\n[2026-04-29T10:48:00Z] Kofi Mensah: Yep, I'll loop Hannah in this week.\n[2026-04-29T10:48:00Z] Amara Singh: Perfect. Quick sanity check on action items — Rosa: money order and escrow deposit Friday, proof to the clinic, tell Kofi about any repairs. Kofi: exhibit set by Friday, escrow tracking today, signed verification, docketing with Hannah. Me: I'll draft the answer and counterclaim for filing by May 6 and update Daniel on the plan. Anything I'm missing?\n[2026-04-29T10:50:00Z] Rosa Delgado: I think that covers it.\n[2026-04-29T10:50:00Z] Kofi Mensah: One thing — do we want to set a formal check-in cadence between now and May 14? I'd suggest weekly given how much we have to land before the hearing.\n[2026-04-29T10:51:00Z] Amara Singh: Good call. Same time next Wednesday, and I'll keep this slot held through May 13.\n[2026-04-29T10:51:00Z] Kofi Mensah: Works.\n[2026-04-29T10:51:00Z] Rosa Delgado: Works.\n[2026-04-29T10:52:00Z] Amara Singh: One more thing while I have you both — on scope, are we still aligned that this case is the nonpayment defense and the habitability counterclaim, and that a separate repair action or a retaliation claim waits until after the hearing? I don't want us to take on more than we can prove by May 14.\n[2026-04-29T10:53:00Z] Rosa Delgado: Understood. Just the defense and counterclaim for now. If things get worse after the hearing we can talk about the rest then.\n[2026-04-29T10:53:00Z] Kofi Mensah: Same.\n[2026-04-29T10:54:00Z] Amara Singh: Great. And on what we keep building before the hearing — updated dated photos of the ceiling and the tub, and a request for a code enforcement re-inspection. Anything else you think we should capture?\n[2026-04-29T10:55:00Z] Rosa Delgado: I could keep a daily temperature log with the thermometer Kofi gave me — just the morning and evening reading, every day until the hearing.\n[2026-04-29T10:55:00Z] Kofi Mensah: Plus one on that. Easy to do, and judges like it.\n[2026-04-29T10:56:00Z] Amara Singh: Added. So ongoing evidence: dated photos, re-inspection request, daily temperature log. Rosa, please start the